{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/focusmode_entry

    The way into focus mode from the ordinary skin of an activity page that can switch in place.

    A form and not a link, because pressing it changes state: the session key is what
    makes that safe, and a bare link which flipped a session flag is the shape a link
    prefetcher walks into. The theme_dimensions/focusmode module intercepts the submit and
    switches in place; without JavaScript the form records the choice and reloads the activity.
    It is in the navbar on a page that opens focused too, where the navbar is hidden: it is the
    way back in after leaving in place. The theme's core renderer splices the rendered form into the
    navbar's plugin output, immediately before the notifications container.

    The label is the accessible name at every width and is only hidden from view below the
    medium breakpoint, where the navbar has no room for it. The icon is raw Font Awesome
    because core's icon map has no reading glyph.

    Context variables required for this template (described without braces, because a
    Mustache comment closes at the first pair of closing braces it meets):

    * actionurl - the theme's focus endpoint the form posts to
    * sesskey - the session key
    * cmid - the course module the learner is opening in focus mode
    * label - the visible text, and the accessible name at every width
    * title - the tooltip

    Example context (json):
    {
        "actionurl": "https://example.com/theme/dimensions/focus.php",
        "sesskey": "AbC123dEf4",
        "cmid": 4,
        "label": "Focus mode",
        "title": "Open this activity in focus mode"
    }
}}
<form class="dimensions-focus-entry d-flex align-items-center" method="post" action="{{actionurl}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="cmid" value="{{cmid}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="action" value="enter">
    <button type="submit" class="btn dimensions-focus-entry-button" data-action="dimensions-focus-enter" title="{{title}}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-book-open-reader" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="d-none d-md-inline dimensions-focus-entry-label">{{label}}</span>
        <span class="visually-hidden d-md-none">{{label}}</span>
    </button>
</form>
